       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 600 mg is three times the 200 mg/day maximum, and you haven't given me a clinical reason for it, such as a documented regimen. A medical student's confirmation also isn't the same as prescriber verification of an out-of-range dose.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Talk to your resident or attending.** If they want a supratherapeutic dose, they can enter it themselves or tell you the rationale. Pharmacy will probably want to review it.\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** I can enter 50 mg, or up to 200 mg, once daily by mouth so the patient isn't left without a plan.\n- **Enter it with a note, once a prescriber has approved it.** If your attending confirms the dose and gives a rationale, tell me and I'll include that in the order note.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
